Third-party notices
===================

PDFium
------

The viewer shows PDF files with PDFium, the PDF library of the Chromium project
(Copyright The PDFium Authors; BSD 3-Clause and Apache 2.0, https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium/).
It is not part of this source tree: a program that ships the viewer puts the library beside its
executable, with the licence texts, using tools/fetch_pdfium.py.

The build used is the one published at https://github.com/bblanchon/pdfium-binaries
(the packaging is Copyright Benoit Blanchon, MIT licence), release chromium/8165,
PDFium 160.0.8165.0, in its variant without V8 and without XFA. The release is immutable and carries
the attestation of GitHub; the SHA-256 of each archive and of each library is written in
pdfium.json and checked when the library is fetched and again before it is loaded.

The library includes other software, each under its own licence, whose texts come in the folder
"licenses" of the archive (fetch_pdfium.py writes them to pdfium-licenses): Abseil, AGG 2.3,
Dragonbox, fast_float, FreeType, HarfBuzz, Highway, ICU, Little CMS, libjpeg-turbo, OpenJPEG,
libpng, LLVM libc, simdutf and zlib. A program that ships the library ships that folder too.

Two of them ask to be named in the documentation of a program that ships them:

  Portions of this software are copyright The FreeType Project (https://freetype.org).
  All rights reserved.

  This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

Rust crates
-----------

libloading (ISC licence) loads the library. image (MIT or Apache 2.0), with the decoders it brings
(png, zune-jpeg, gif, image-webp), reads the pictures. zip (MIT) reads the office archives, sha2
(MIT or Apache 2.0) checks the library, egui (MIT or Apache 2.0) draws the panel.
